<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_TibannaTap_BeldonWiring.xml        UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F2
  ============================================================================
  Wires the F2 spike class (RM_CompGatherableGas, already compiling,
  src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/RM_CompGatherableGas.cs) onto
  the actual shipped Beldon — forge_kit_spec.md F2's own text: "a def named
  Beldon already ships in the mod set... this kit attaches the comp to
  whatever kind the roster lands; it ships no PawnKindDef."

  The Beldon def as shipped: RSW_Beldon
  (src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RSW_Beldon.xml,
  MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Wave C — a port from mlie.starwarsanimalcollection
  renamed under this repo's OWN RSW_ tier, not a donor/vendor mod's file we
  don't control). Patched rather than hand-edited directly even though it is
  repo-owned: RSW_Beldon.xml is generic RimStarWars-tier content ("any Star
  Wars scenario"), and the tibanna tap is Utinni-tier campaign mechanics
  (§8's Empire monopoly) — baking a Forge-specific comp straight into the
  shared SWBestiary file would leak campaign content into the generic tier,
  same discipline RUT_ForgePulse_BiomeWiring.xml (F1, this same item)
  already applied to RUT_TheForge itself. PatchOperationAdd targets
  RSW_Beldon's own existing <comps> node (already carries EggLayer +
  Milkable) rather than replacing it.

  Gate: PatchOperationFindMod on the kit's display name. ⚠️ MayRequire on
  an <Operation> is INERT — MEASURED 2026-09-17 against 1.6 source
  (ModContentPack.LoadPatches ignores the attribute; PatchOperation has no
  such field). The un-gated injection discarded ALL of RSW_Beldon.xml on
  the full-list load: a missing <li Class="..."> type discards the whole
  FILE, not just the parent def. FindMod is the only real per-operation
  gate; without the kit this whole operation is now a true no-op.

  Tuning: interval 2 days, amount 12 — forge_kit_spec.md F2's own INVENTED
  values, verbatim ("interval 2 days, amount 12 RUT_TibannaGas"). gatherDef
  points at RUT_TibannaGas.xml (this same pass). fullnessLabelKey repoints
  the comp's default "RM_GasPressure" generic key to the concrete
  "tibanna pressure" flavor the kit spec's own text names for the inspect
  line (RUT_TibannaPressure, Languages/English/Keyed/
  RUT_Forge_Mechanics.xml, this same pass).

  Sex-independent per the comp's own design (no milkFemaleOnly-equivalent
  gate) — nothing in this patch changes that.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: Environmental Hazards Kit</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="RSW_Beldon"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_GatherableGas">
          <gatherIntervalDays>2</gatherIntervalDays>
          <gatherAmount>12</gatherAmount>
          <gatherDef>RUT_TibannaGas</gatherDef>
          <fullnessLabelKey>RUT_TibannaPressure</fullnessLabelKey>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
